raylib
------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

  Unlike a source dependency, this project REDISTRIBUTES prebuilt raylib
  5.5.0 binaries under libs/ (macOS, Linux x86-64/i386, Windows 32/64-bit for
  MSVC and MinGW-w64), so an example runs without a system raylib install.
  Those binaries are raylib's own release artifacts, unmodified. The zlib
  license permits this provided the notice is retained — which is what this
  section is.

  Many examples under src/examples/ are Clojure ports of raylib's own example
  programs. docs/guide/example-catalog.md names the upstream C source for each
  (e.g. core/core_basic_window, shapes/shapes_bouncing_ball). Those examples
  are zlib/libpng licensed at their origin. zlib is permissive and imposes no
  reciprocal obligation, so distributing those ports within an EPL-2.0 project
  is fine; their upstream origin is recorded per example so the attribution
  stays traceable.


